              "# China’s yuan falls to lowest level of 2018, suffering longest losing streak in two years\n### Analysts see it slipping further as the China-US trade dispute shows no signs of easing and the central bank signals it will let the currency weaken more\n3-MIN READ 3-MIN\n\nAnalysts expect it to slip further, down to between 6.55 and 6.6 in the near future.",
              "Published: 11:00am, 25 Jun 2018 Updated: 11:30pm, 25 Jun 2018\n\nChina’s yuan suffered its longest losing streak in two years, falling for an eighth straight session early on Monday to its lowest level of 2018",
